# augustl.com

The live site is a Next.js app deployed on Vercel.

## Development

Install the toolchain declared in `mise.toml`, then install dependencies and run
Next.js:

```sh
mise install
mise run setup
mise run dev
```

With the mise shell hook enabled, entering the repository automatically selects
Node 24.11.0 and Yarn 1.22.22. The `mise run` commands also guarantee the pinned
versions even when another executable appears earlier in `PATH`.

The development site is available at <http://localhost:7010>. Production builds use:

```sh
mise run build
mise run start
```

Vercel detects the Next.js app directly; no static export step is needed.

## Posts

Posts live below `posts/` as plain `.md` files with YAML frontmatter:

```md
---
title: "A post title"
date: "2026-08-30"
content_format: "markdown"
archive_order: 0
---

Post contents go here.
```

`content_format` is either `markdown` or `html`. The latter preserves the markup
of older posts byte-for-byte inside a Markdown file. `archive_order` preserves the
historic ordering of posts that share a publication date; lower numbers appear
first. Optional legacy fields are `updated`, `series`, `rss_warning`, and
`unlisted`.

## Parity testing

Given an archived export of the previous site, compare every post, page shell,
and Atom feed with the Next.js production build:

```sh
yarn check:parity /path/to/legacy-export
```

The parity suite uses the system Chromium browser.
